      "role": "user",
      "content": "i see. so if we say their actions were a \"necessary response\" to the colonial system, does that mean the British side of the argument—like the idea that they were maintaining law and order or protecting citizens—doesn't actually hold any moral weight? like, was there any legitimate way for the colonial government to exist there, or was the whole system so fundamentally broken that any attempt to uphold it was automatically wrong?",
